[[Alaska]] first required its residents to register their [[motor vehicle]]s and display [[Vehicle registration plate|license plates]] in 1921, while still an [[Organized incorporated territories of the United States|organized incorporated territory of the United States]]. It was admitted to the Union as the 49th state in January 1959.

{{As of|2023}}, plates are issued by the [[Alaska Department of Administration]] through its Division of Motor Vehicles. Only rear plates have been required for standard passenger vehicles since August 11, 2022.<ref name=autogenerated>https://www.facebook.com/AlaskaDMV/posts/pfbid02xQPmwMYLV63MrQdjBTU2U1uLdF2PvhGnw4zEyWdkkrqhVwS9zovWBp2Df4wmw7T4l {{User-generated source|certain=yes|date=August 2022}}</ref> On vehicles with two license plates, only the rear plate is required to be stickered.<ref name=autogenerated1>http://www.state.ak.us/dmv/plates/index.htm Alaska DMV License Plates</ref>

